"comparison": "Micron and AMD share an identical structure for their voluntary redemption pricing, specifically using the 'greater of' test between 100% of principal and the present value of remaining payments. AMD states redemption at 'the greater of the present value of the principal amount and future interest... or 100% of the principal amount' (mu_2024_8_P056_S001 parallels this with 'greater of (i) 100% of the principal amount... and (ii) the present value of the remaining scheduled payments'). However, Micron includes a distinct provision allowing redemption at par value between one and six months prior to maturity, a feature not disclosed in AMD's excerpt for these specific notes. Regarding change of control, AMD specifies the 101% repurchase price explicitly in the cited text, while Micron references the requirement in a separate covenant section.",
